                        "entry_id": "4f7ff61d-7991-32a4-b25c-879e78555790",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person involved in blackbirding (kidnapping Pacific islanders as cheap labour)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a04bbaa7-fb71-49b0-9820-8f6d4240c1aa",
                                "sense_id": "83774610-a0fc-3753-9dcc-0f388c38f8bb",
                                "text": "The renaming of New South Wales’s Ben Boyd National Park — named for Australia’s first blackbirder — as Beowa National Park in 2022 was a good first step. But apologising for running a slave trade that tore tens of thousands of Pacific islanders from their families should not be a hard sell in Australia’s parliament."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8044d6b0-14a2-3707-9552-739b1b68f062",
                        "entry_id": "4f7ff61d-7991-32a4-b25c-879e78555790",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A ship used for blackbirding; a slaver."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b3299013-f29b-3725-924a-56e8354c09b8",
                        "entry_id": "4f7ff61d-7991-32a4-b25c-879e78555790",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A slavecatcher"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "97cc31f1-17c6-4e7f-ae61-c22cd5fb8a13",
                                "sense_id": "b3299013-f29b-3725-924a-56e8354c09b8",
                                "text": "Runaway slaves and free blacks were constantly being kidnapped by New York City’s many “Blackbirders,” slave-catching bounty hunters who deported their captures to the plantations."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
